{"name":"Composed","hex":"#bbc8b2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"composed","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Showing composure."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of compose"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/composed"}],"entries":[{"title":"Choreography","blocks":[{"text":"Choreography is the art of designing sequences of movements of physical bodies in which motion or form or both are specified. Choreography may also refer to the design itself. A choreographer creates choreographies through the art of choreography, a process known as choreographing. It most commonly refers to dance choreography."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Zorn_Cachucha.jpg/330px-Zorn_Cachucha.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Choreography"},{"title":"Composition (language)","blocks":[{"text":"The term composition as it refers to writing, can describe authors' decisions about, processes for designing, and sometimes the final product of, a composed linguistic work. In original use, it tended to describe practices concerning the development of oratorical performances, and eventually essays, narratives, or genres of imaginative literature, but since the mid-20th century emergence of the field of composition studies, its use has broadened to apply to any composed work: print or digital, alphanumeric or multimodal. As such, the composition of linguistic works goes beyond the exclusivity of written and oral documents to visual and digital arenas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Leaf_a2r_of_an_incunable_edition_of_Aristotle%27s_Rhetoric_%28Venice-_Filippo_di_Pietro%2C_22_June_1481%3B_ISTC_ia01046000%29.jpg/330px-Leaf_a2r_of_an_incunable_edition_of_Aristotle%27s_Rhetoric_%28Venice-_Filippo_di_Pietro%2C_22_June_1481%3B_ISTC_ia01046000%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Composition_(language)"},{"title":"Composed (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Composed is the second studio album by Sacramento born musician, composer and arranger Jherek Bischoff. It was released by The Leaf Label and Brassland. The album features nine orchestral pieces with a different vocalist on eight of the nine tracks."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/32/Jherek_Bischoff_%E2%80%93_Composed.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Composed_(album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Choreographic_document_of_dances_in_Catalonia_in_1496_manuscrit_de_Cervera.jpg/500px-Choreographic_document_of_dances_in_Catalonia_in_1496_manuscrit_de_Cervera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Choreographic_document_of_dances_in_Catalonia_in_1496_manuscrit_de_Cervera.jpg/1280px-Choreographic_document_of_dances_in_Catalonia_in_1496_manuscrit_de_Cervera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Choreographic_document_of_dances_in_Catalonia_in_1496_manuscrit_de_Cervera.jpg/500px-Choreographic_document_of_dances_in_Catalonia_in_1496_manuscrit_de_Cervera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"One of the first documents with choreographic signs is the Catalan manuscript of Cervera from 1496","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChoreographic_document_of_dances_in_Catalonia_in_1496_manuscrit_de_Cervera.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Martin_Luther_King_Jr._-_I_Have_A_Dream_Speech.jpg/500px-Martin_Luther_King_Jr._-_I_Have_A_Dream_Speech.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=par